DRAFT — not built, not tested, not in any build (2026-10-11)

What this is: the changes pmos/linux-google-steelhead/APKBUILD and
kernel/configs/steelhead_defconfig would need to build the PowerVR SGX540
kernel driver (openpvrsgx DDK 1.17.4948957, module pvrsrvkm_omap4_sgx540_120)
IN-TREE as a module, inside the kernel package. It is a fragment: only the
parts that change are shown, against the APKBUILD as of dc988b9
(pkgver 6.18.48, pkgrel 20). Nothing here has been compiled; the compile gate
(groundwork §4 Phase 1 step 1, kdp §12 step 1) is what turns it into a fact.

Short names below follow the master note
(docs/2026-10-11-gpu-sgx540-groundwork.md): kdp = kernel-driver-port.md,
pm = power-clocks-pm.md, ur = usecases-roadmap.md, ub = userspace-blobs.md,
ml = mainline-6.18.md.


== 1. Why in-tree, in THIS package, with no subpackage ==================

- nq-kernel-ota stage-apk copies /lib/modules/<rel> ONLY out of the kernel
  apk (userspace/nexusq-kernel-ota/nq-kernel-ota:398-415, read 2026-10-11).
  A separate module aport, or a subpackage of this one, would be missing on
  every kernel OTA and would not roll back with the slot [kdp §6.1, ur §5.3,
  groundwork §1 "Boot image" row].
- CONFIG_MODVERSIONS=y (steelhead_defconfig:695) plus
  CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-r$pkgrel" (APKBUILD:97-113) make an out-of-tree module
  a lockstep rebuild per pkgrel, and we ship no kernel -dev package
  (APKBUILD:126-138) [kdp §6.1].
- Built-in (=y) is "very likely not viable": ~66 KB of LZMA text alone for
  the stock 1.8 KM against ~92-94 KB boot-image headroom [kdp §6.1,
  Verification item 2]. =m leaves the zImage unchanged.

=> package() does NOT split. The .ko lands under
   /lib/modules/<rel>/kernel/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/... of the main package
   and travels with the kernel slot.


