== 3. source= additions =================================================

The archive is the whole openpvrsgx kernel tree. UNVERIFIED: ~230-260 MB
gz [kdp §6.2 item 1]; pmbootstrap caches distfiles, so it is paid once per
pin. Only drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/{Kconfig,Makefile,pvr-drv.c,pvr-drv.h,
1.17.4948957/} is used (≈6.0 MB, 358 files) [kdp §6.2]. The smaller
alternative (a script-generated pvrsgx-<sha>.tar.xz release asset) adds a
mirror we would have to keep honest [kdp §6.2]; not chosen here.

The patch names are PROPOSALS, numbered after the DT draft 0062. Letters
are kdp §8's patch set; groundwork §2 counts (a)-(g) as "our 7 patches",
(h) is the hook and (i) the cherry-pick.

```
_pvrsgx_commit=d2f1e031d58aca97bc4b62367f0d7bef4a7559c3	# pvrsrvkm-6.18-rc6
_pvrsgx_ddk=1.17.4948957

source="
	https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/linux-$pkgver.tar.xz
	linux_openpvrsgx-$_pvrsgx_commit.tar.gz::https://github.com/openpvrsgx-devgroup/linux_openpvrsgx/archive/$_pvrsgx_commit.tar.gz
	$_config
	0001-ASoC-tas571x-add-TAS5713-support.patch
	...
	0061-mfd-twl6030-irq-map-every-PIH-bit-so-an-unclaimed-one-is-not-an-error.patch
	0062-ARM-dts-omap4-steelhead-run-the-SGX-from-DPLL_PER-like-stock.patch
	0063-drm-hook-the-pvrsgx-directory-into-the-DRM-Kconfig-and-Makefile.patch        # (h)
	0064-drm-pvrsgx-1.17-use-VMAP-mem-areas-on-OMAP.patch                             # (a)
	0065-drm-pvrsgx-1.17-allocate-cached-areas-with-__vmalloc.patch                   # (b)
	0066-drm-pvrsgx-1.17-OMAP4-SGX540-sysconfig-at-stock-timing.patch                 # (c)
	0067-drm-pvrsgx-balance-runtime-PM-in-pvr_probe-and-fix-the-remove-order.patch    # (d)
	0068-drm-pvrsgx-1.17-map-dma-buf-attachments-with-the-unlocked-helpers.patch      # (e)
	0069-drm-pvrsgx-build-the-OMAP4470-SGX544-variant-only-on-request.patch           # (f)
	0070-drm-pvrsgx-drop-select-DRM_LEGACY.patch                                      # (g)
	0071-drm-pvrsgx-1.17-initialise-blocking_fence_count.patch                        # (i) ff422e4ab0bb
"
```

(The "# (x)" annotations are for this draft only; source= must not carry
comments.)

What each patch carries, with the evidence it rests on:

  (h) `source "drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/Kconfig"` + `obj-y += pvrsgx/` in
      drivers/gpu/drm/{Kconfig,Makefile}: the merge diff without the
      DRM_INTEL_CDV line [kdp §8 h]. The only patch that touches pristine
      files, so it is the only one that would apply without the prepare()
      copy below.
  (a) -DPVR_LINUX_MEM_AREA_USE_VMAP for the OMAP SGX540 build. Without it
      SGXInitialise times out (openpvrsgx #3, kc1 #26, TI eda7780bfd52);
      absent from the 6.18-rc6 and 7.2 Makefiles [kdp §3.1, §8 a].
  (b) _VMallocWrapper(): PAGE_KERNEL -> __vmalloc(); removes the need for
      EXPORT_SYMBOL(__vmalloc_node_range_noprof), so no core-mm patch.
      Statically verified single call chain [kdp §8 b, Verification 11].
  (c) sysconfig-omap4.h for SGX540 rev 120: SYS_SGX_CLOCK_SPEED 307200000,
      HW recovery 100 Hz, PDS timer 1000 Hz, APM latency 100 ms (stock
      sgx_apm_latency @0xc0725b9c); today OMAP4 silently uses the AM437x
      header (200 MHz / 50 Hz / 2 ms) [kdp §8 c, pm open question 3,
      groundwork §2 table]. If Phase 0 forces 153.6 MHz (VDD_CORE gate),
      SYS_SGX_CLOCK_SPEED must say 153600000 instead, or be taken from
      clk_get_rate() [pm open question 3].
  (d) pm_runtime_use_autosuspend() + 100 ms delay + put_autosuspend() after
      drm_dev_register() in pvr_probe(); pvr_remove() order
      drm_dev_unregister -> unload -> drm_dev_put. Code inference with one
      piece of counter-evidence (84db121f1016) [kdp §8 d, pm TL;DR 8,
      groundwork §5 P1].
  (e) dma_buf_map_attachment_unlocked()/..._unmap_..._unlocked() at
      dmabuf.c:186 and :101 [kdp §7 6.2 row, §8 e].
  (f) Kconfig bool SGX_OMAP4470 (default n) gating the second
      pvrsrvkm_omap4_sgx544_112 build under ARCH_OMAP4 (Makefile:92-100)
      [kdp §8 f].
  (g) remove `select DRM_LEGACY` from SGX_DRM (Kconfig:69); the symbol does
      not exist in 6.18.48 [kdp §8 g].
  (i) cherry-pick ff422e4ab0bb from -v3 [kdp §3.2, §8 i].

Patch generation (project rule, .claude/rules/kernel.md): patches come from
the git patch stack with `git format-patch` and must apply with GNU patch on
a pristine tree. ASSUMED workflow, UNVERIFIED against how the kstack tree
(~/nexusq-build/kstack/linux on the build machine [kdp §12 step 1]) is
organised: one LOCAL commit "import pvrsgx @ d2f1e031" that copies exactly
the files prepare() copies, which is never exported; (h) and (a)-(i) are
exported on top of it. GNU patch then sees the same pre-image that prepare()
creates.


== 4. prepare(): copy before patching ===================================

Ordering matters: (a)-(g) and (i) patch files that only exist after the copy,
so the copy runs BEFORE default_prepare [kdp §6.2 item 2].

```
prepare() {
	# PowerVR SGX KM (openpvrsgx, DDK $_pvrsgx_ddk), built in-tree as a module.
	# Copy exactly the driver directory from the pinned upstream tree before the
	# patches run: our pvrsgx patches apply to these files. The base commit is
	# tracked in git as $_pvrsgx_commit; scripts/pvrsgx-bump.sh is the update path.
	# docs/2026-10-11-gpu-sgx540-groundwork.md
	_pvr_src="$srcdir/linux_openpvrsgx-$_pvrsgx_commit/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx"
	_pvr_dst="$builddir/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx"
	[ -d "$_pvr_src/$_pvrsgx_ddk" ] || die "openpvrsgx archive has no pvrsgx/$_pvrsgx_ddk"
	[ -e "$_pvr_dst" ] && die "pristine tree already has drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx"
	mkdir -p "$_pvr_dst"
	cp -a "$_pvr_src/Kconfig" "$_pvr_src/Makefile" \
		"$_pvr_src/pvr-drv.c" "$_pvr_src/pvr-drv.h" \
		"$_pvr_src/$_pvrsgx_ddk" "$_pvr_dst/"

	default_prepare
	cp "$srcdir/$_config" .config

	sed -i "s/^CONFIG_LOCALVERSION=.*/CONFIG_LOCALVERSION=\"-r$pkgrel\"/" .config
}
```

Assumptions:
- abuild's default unpack extracts the .tar.gz to
  $srcdir/linux_openpvrsgx-<full sha>/ (GitHub archive layout). UNVERIFIED for
  this exact archive; the `[ -d ]` guard makes a different layout fail loudly.
- The extraction of a full second kernel tree costs disk and time in the
  builder container (UNVERIFIED size). A custom unpack() that extracts only
  */drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/* would avoid it; not drafted, because it would
  re-implement abuild's unpack for the kernel tarball too.
- The `[ -e "$_pvr_dst" ] && die` guard is there because a future mainline
  that ships its own drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx must be noticed, not overwritten.


== 5. build(): fail loudly if olddefconfig dropped a symbol =============

olddefconfig silently drops a symbol whose Kconfig is missing (e.g. if (h)
did not apply). Add after the olddefconfig call, before `make`:

```
	# The GPU KM must survive olddefconfig. A missing pvrsgx Kconfig (hook
	# patch not applied) drops these silently and the image ships without the
	# module.
	for _sym in CONFIG_SGX=y CONFIG_PVRSGX_1_17_4948957=y CONFIG_SGX_DRM=y \
			CONFIG_SGX_OMAP=m; do
		grep -qx "$_sym" .config || die "olddefconfig dropped $_sym"
	done
	# osfunc.c:126-135 has an #error for a non-preemptible kernel; catch it here
	# with a readable message instead of 20 minutes into the build.
	grep -Eqx 'CONFIG_PREEMPT(_VOLUNTARY)?=y' .config \
		|| die "pvrsgx 1.17 needs CONFIG_PREEMPT_VOLUNTARY=y or CONFIG_PREEMPT=y"
```

The second check is redundant with the compiler's #error by design: it is
the readable failure, and it is the test that can be seen failing first
(groundwork §4 Phase 1a: "the compile gate fails with the #error on the old
config and passes on the new").


== 6. package(): assert the module is there, no split ====================

Add after `make zinstall modules_install dtbs_install ...`:

```
	# The SGX540 KM is part of THIS package on purpose: nq-kernel-ota carries
	# /lib/modules/<rel> only from the kernel apk. Never split it out.
	_rel=$(cat "$builddir"/include/config/kernel.release)
	_ko=$(find "$pkgdir/lib/modules/$_rel" -name pvrsrvkm_omap4_sgx540_120.ko)
	[ -n "$_ko" ] || die "pvrsrvkm_omap4_sgx540_120.ko missing from the package"
	[ -z "$(find "$pkgdir/lib/modules/$_rel" -name 'pvrsrvkm_omap4_sgx544_*.ko')" ] \
		|| die "the OMAP4470 SGX544 variant was built (patch f not effective)"
```

- Expected path, from Maemo's 6.18.51 package: .../kernel/drivers/gpu/drm/
  pvrsgx/1.17.4948957/eurasia_km/pvrsrvkm_omap4_sgx540_120.ko [ub §2.2];
  `find` is used so a different sub-path does not matter.
- INSTALL_MOD_STRIP=1 stays: the KM is GPL/MIT source we build, stripping it
  is fine (the TI userspace is a different matter, see sgx-ddk-um.APKBUILD.draft).
- The module carries MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of) for ti,omap4430-gpu (expected
  modinfo alias `of:N*T*Cti,omap4430-gpu*` [kdp §12 step 1]), so udev would
  autoload it at boot. Until patch (d) is proven on hardware it must not
  autoload [groundwork §5 P1/P11, §7]. See §8 of this draft.


== 7. defconfig (kernel/configs/steelhead_defconfig) ===================

The aport copies the defconfig verbatim into config-google-steelhead.armv7
(docker-build.sh:285-286, scripts/build-kernel-boot.sh:51-52), so the change
is an edit of that file, not a merged fragment. The file is a full .config
(it carries "# end of" markers); after the first olddefconfig with the new
symbols, copy the resulting .config back so diffs stay readable [kdp open
question 10].

7a. Preemption model. Its OWN kernel revision, Phase 1a, before the GPU
    revision [groundwork §4 Phase 1a, §5 P2]. Today (steelhead_defconfig:99-102):

```
CONFIG_PREEMPT_NONE_BUILD=y
CONFIG_PREEMPT_NONE=y
# CONFIG_PREEMPT_VOLUNTARY is not set
# CONFIG_PREEMPT is not set
```

    Variant V (upstream's choice, 0affbb5a7b95 / omap2plus_defconfig:511):

```
# CONFIG_PREEMPT_NONE is not set
CONFIG_PREEMPT_VOLUNTARY=y
# CONFIG_PREEMPT is not set
```

    Variant P (stock parity: 3.0.8 "#1 SMP PREEMPT"; the working kc1 run):

```
# CONFIG_PREEMPT_NONE is not set
# CONFIG_PREEMPT_VOLUNTARY is not set
CONFIG_PREEMPT=y
```

    The *_BUILD helper symbol is recomputed by olddefconfig. Whether
    VOLUNTARY is enough for the DDK's spin-wait-on-workqueue paths is
    UNVERIFIED [kdp §8 k, groundwork §8 q5]; the choice is made on the
    Phase 1a A/B (measurement-protocol.md, arm P1a) and recorded in a dated
    note. Variant P adds "preempt" to the module vermagic [kdp §8 k];
    harmless here because every module is rebuilt in-tree.

7b. The SGX symbols, base = pvrsrvkm-6.18-rc6 [kdp §9]:

```
CONFIG_SGX=y
CONFIG_PVRSGX_1_17_4948957=y
# CONFIG_SGX_DEBUG is not set
CONFIG_SGX_DRM=y
CONFIG_SGX_OMAP=m
# CONFIG_SGX_GENERIC is not set
# CONFIG_SGX_OMAP4470 is not set
```

    CONFIG_SGX is a bool that only gates the subdirectory; with SGX_OMAP=m
    nothing is built into the zImage [kdp §6.1]. CONFIG_SGX_OMAP4470 exists
    only once patch (f) is in.

7c. ONLY if the base becomes -v3/-v4 (fallback F2): pin the ABI symbols so
    the UM build-options check cannot drift [kdp §3.2, §9]:

```
CONFIG_SGX_ABI=y
CONFIG_PVRSGX_1_17_4948957_ABI=y
CONFIG_SGX_PB_PER_CONTEXT=y
CONFIG_SGX_HW_PERF=y
CONFIG_SGX_HW_RECOVERY=y
# CONFIG_SGX_PDUMP is not set
# CONFIG_SGX_HW_PROFILING is not set
# CONFIG_SGX_USSE_EDM_STATUS_DEBUG is not set
CONFIG_SGX_IOCTL_ALIAS=0
```

7d. Already present and sufficient, no change [kdp §9]: CONFIG_DRM=y (2830),
    CONFIG_DRM_OMAP=y (2869), CONFIG_DMA_SHARED_BUFFER=y (1425),
    CONFIG_CMA=y with CMA_SIZE_MBYTES=16 (5529; Maemo uses 32, 16 assumed
    enough because omapdrm scans out through DMM/TILER [ur §6 Phase 0 step 5,
    groundwork §5 P15]), CONFIG_MODVERSIONS=y (695), CONFIG_WERROR off (33).

7e. Not now: CONFIG_PM_DEVFREQ / DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND /
    DEVFREQ_THERMAL belong to optional Phase 7 [groundwork §4 Phase 7,
    pm §10].


== 8. Autoload: a kernel-side blacklist that travels with the slot =====

The roadmap ships /etc/modprobe.d/nexusq-gpu.conf with
`blacklist pvrsrvkm_omap4_sgx540_120` in device-google-steelhead
[groundwork §4 Phase 1 step 3, ur §6 Phase 1 step 2]. That file lives on the
ROOTFS, while the module arrives with the KERNEL slot. A unit whose rootfs
does not yet carry the blacklist but which takes a GPU kernel by OTA would
autoload the module at boot, exactly risk P11 [groundwork §5].

Proposal (not in the notes; UNVERIFIED): ALSO add
`modprobe.blacklist=pvrsrvkm_omap4_sgx540_120` to CONFIG_CMDLINE
(steelhead_defconfig:489). With CONFIG_CMDLINE_FORCE=y (:492) the command
line is part of the kernel image, so the blacklist rides the same slot as
the module and rolls back with it. kmod reads `modprobe.blacklist=` from the
kernel command line, and a blacklist only suppresses alias-based loading,
so an explicit `modprobe pvrsrvkm_omap4_sgx540_120` in Phase 1 still works
(kmod behaviour as documented in modprobe.d(5); UNVERIFIED on the unit:
check `lsmod` after boot and one explicit modprobe). Remove it in the
kernel revision that introduces the Phase 6 boot guard.


== 9. pkgrel, CHANGELOG, tests =========================================

- Three separate kernel revisions, each its own pkgrel bump and CHANGELOG
  line naming the revision (.claude/rules/aports.md):
    r(N)    0062 DT clock block (Phase 0; inert in power terms)
    r(N+1)  preemption model (Phase 1a)
    r(N+2)  pvrsgx import + 0063-0071 + SGX symbols + cmdline blacklist
            (Phase 1)
  N is whatever pkgrel follows 20 at adoption time. Each revision gets its
  own /lib/modules/6.18.48-r<N> through LOCALVERSION (APKBUILD:97-113).
- tests/test_aports.py keeps passing: its sources() filter drops entries
  containing "://" (the archive), and every new kernel/patches/*.patch is
  listed in source= (sources() at test_aports.py:28-34, the patch test at
  :38-48).
- scripts/pvrsgx-bump.sh <branch|sha> (to be written, [kdp §6.2 item 4]):
  resolves the upstream head with git ls-remote, rewrites _pvrsgx_commit,
  runs `pmbootstrap checksum`, extracts a pristine 6.18.x + the new pvrsgx
  tree and re-applies 0063-0071 with GNU patch; any reject fails loudly.
  Its own seen-failing test: point it at a commit where one of our patches
  no longer applies and watch it exit non-zero [kdp §12 step 4].
- sha512sums: regenerated by the build (`pmbootstrap checksum`), never hand
  edited (.claude/rules/aports.md). The archive gets a real sha512 (not
  SKIP), like nexusq-glibc-rt pins its tarball (pmos/nexusq-glibc-rt/APKBUILD).
- Review gates before any commit under kernel/ or pmos/: stock-parity-auditor
  for (c) and the DT block, fleet-safety-reviewer (CLAUDE.md agent table).


== 10. What this fragment does not decide ===============================

- VOLUNTARY vs PREEMPT (Phase 1a data).
- 307.2 vs 153.6 MHz (Phase 0 VDD_CORE measurement; patch (c) and the 0062
  DT block must agree) [pm §4 Gate].
- Whether the live match table is pvr-drv.c's ti,omap4430-gpu or the DDK's
  PVR_USE_DEVICE_TREE ti,omap4-sgx540-120 [groundwork §8 q9]; this draft
  assumes pvr-drv.c, like the notes.
- Whether d2f1e031 compiles unchanged on 6.18.48 with Alpine GCC 15.2
  [groundwork §8 q8, §5 P16]; budget +0-8 h [kdp §12 step 1].
